### 3. Commercial Use Restriction

Use of the Software for **Commercial Purposes** (as defined in Sections 2 and 2A) generally requires a separate, written Commercial License agreement with Licensor, **except** as expressly permitted in:

* **Section 2A(a)** — commercial use of Oxiverse hosted APIs/services by independent consumers does not require a Commercial License; and
* **Section 2A(d)** — qualifying open-source projects may receive a free Commercial License after contacting Oxiverse.

To inquire about Commercial Licensing, contact: **[likhith@oxiverse.com](mailto:likhith@oxiverse.com)**

Commercial Licenses may include terms for:

* Self-hosted deployment — permitted for Non-Commercial Purposes only under this License; Licensor does not grant Commercial Licenses for self-hosted commercial use (see Section 2A(b))
* White-labeling or redistribution rights
* Support, updates, and SLA options
* Custom feature development or integration

